  "findings": [
    "Baseline keeps one IllagerVoiceManager and its Pillager reachable for every illager that ever ticked (200 after kill and churn).",
    "Baseline keeps the pre-portal Pillager reachable after a dimension change (202 live = 200 dead + old + new copy), because the manager still holds the old instance.",
    "Patched releases every manager on unload (0 after kill) and every dead Pillager once vanilla drops its tick snapshot (0 after churn).",
    "Patched replaces the traveller's manager with one bound to the Nether copy: 1 manager and 1 live Pillager after the crossing, so the old copy is collectable.",
    "Patched logs the enable line, applies all four mixins, and emits none of the vendor per-illager INFO lines (baseline: 402 over 201 illagers)."
  ],
  "vanilla_retention_note": "Without any mod (Fabric Loader only, and with Fabric API only), the 200 killed pillagers stay reachable after kill, save-all and 60 s. A heap dump traced them to DedicatedServer.levels -> ServerLevel.entityTickList -> EntityTickList.passive: entities removed mid-tick remain in the last copy-on-write snapshot until another entity is added or removed mid-tick. It is bounded to one snapshot and clears on normal churn, so the probe forces one item despawn before counting. This is vanilla behaviour, not part of the IllagerBlabber defect.",
  "not_verified": [
    "Audible voice lines and their playback position on a client after a dimension change",
    "Long-uptime heap behaviour on the live server",
    "Chunk-unload and reload of illagers with players present"
  ]
